detail.abstract:
Digitally governed organizations can still accumulate persistent, high-burden workflows that do not materially improve outcomes participants care about. We formalize this failure mode for settings where task-relevant actions are natively logged, governance is auditable, and decisions must be reproducible from committed observations. To avoid a single fixed welfare function, we introduce Mutable Subjective Objective Registries (MSORs): versioned, anti-retcon dashboards over observable components (leisure, self-preference fulfillment, and social-structural cohesion), with protected experienced-meaning telemetry.&nbsp;
<div>
 Task value is defined by causal contribution, estimated through a tiered identification stack: randomized ablation, quasi-experiments, and observational learning with proximal bridges plus weak-proxy fallback to partial identification. Decisions use a Bayesian state with operational, essential, experiential, and value-certification posteriors (𝑝 bull , 𝑝 ess , 𝑝 exp , 𝑝 val). Essentialness combines observable tail inference (Bayesian EVT/CVaR channels) with a bounded precautionary prior for unobservable existential channels that decays under endogenous structural drift, preventing both reckless deletion and irreversible conservatism.&nbsp;
</div>
<div>
 We replace hard auto-deletion with a burden-of-proof regime: hold → experiment → justify/substitute → reversible throttle. The governance layer includes challenge-bonded contestable ontology updates, anti-collusion risk-bounded substitution contracts, reserve and deficit-ledger solvency controls under systemic shocks, and constitutional sunset/renewal with auditable no-meta self-mutation of hyperparameters. On dependency graphs, we provide safe SCC intervention with fallback artifacts and dense-SCC edge controls that reduce cyclic burden while preserving essential downstream continuity and innovation capacity.&nbsp;
</div>
<div>
 Main guarantees include: non-identifiability without committed registries; resistance of endogenous social weights to coercive bureaucracy, plutocratic concentration, and echo-chamber capture; coalition deterrence under on-log/off-log risk discounting; controlled dynamics under endogenous action-space expansion with explicit phase-threshold conditions; and sublinear dynamic regret for both operational allocation and meta-parameter adaptation. The framework is deployment-oriented: it maps to XES/JXES process-mining logs, private-log public-verifiability releases, attested local execution (TEE/MPC with spot recomputation), and machine-readable claim dependencies for audit and crawler consumption.
</div>

